NAME
    del - delete files

SYNOPSIS
    del name|glob [name|glob ...]

DESCRIPTION
    Deletes each file named. A glob (* or ? in the last component, case
    folded) deletes every matching file in that directory. The file's
    directory entry is tombstoned; its sectors are not reclaimed
    (Y1/OS has no PACK yet). A name that is not a file reports
    "del: not a file: NAME" and the others are still deleted; a glob
    that matches nothing reports "del: no match: GLOB". Files only:
    remove a directory with rmdir. del is /BIN/DEL.

    The shell also has a built-in del, used only when /BIN/DEL is
    missing: one path, no globs, "not a file" when it fails.

LIMITS
    Up to 24 files per glob word.

EXAMPLES
    del /F.TXT
    del A.TXT B.TXT /T/C.TXT
    del /T/*.BAK

NOTES
    Removed from the P8X version: pack (to get the space back) and the
    /d1 mount. New: globs.
    Ported from P8X os/commands/del.c 2026-09-23.

SEE ALSO
    rmdir, mv, touch, globx
